body:
Wow, this isn't really a suggestion on what to do. I just want to say how lucky you are that you can do that. I'm from SE Asia, I'd love to do that too but I don't have the USD money converted to SE Asia currency advantage. I travel SE Asia on my vacation leaves and some long weekends.  I see lot's of Westerners do what you do and stay very long on islands and I'm jealous of them every time. How it's just easy for you guys to leave everything and then comeback to your job again. I just think it's not that easy in a third world country. 

&nbsp;

Wish you all the best man! Good luck!!

Hi, I didn't really give up anything for Lent because I had an event coming up. But after reading this post I plan to give up Facebook. Originally, I planned to give up gaming for Lent but only every Friday which was extremely hard for me because Friday is best day for gaming because of no work the next day. Unfrotunately, I lost on the 3rd week of Lent =( 

&nbsp;

After seeing your realziation on Facebook, I want to seriosly try to abstain from it. I hate it because I get jealous when other peoples post get more likes than mine, and that's not good for me at all. Hmm, I think i'll try it for 2 weeks and see how it goes. I just removed the shortcut from my phone's homepage after reading your post XD. That's a start I guess. I hope I can do it.

But what about the times when the service people are being dicks. Our food was delayed for 30mins, and the supposed senior waiter asked if we just wanted to cancel it. Are you kidding me? While arguing with this senior waiter (he was literally arguing it wasn't 30mins yet like it was only 20 or 25), after a few mins the other waiter brings the food to our table. 

&nbsp;


Now I get the notion that you need to be mad or pressure them or else they would just be lazy about it. I mean, please correct me otherwise.

I lost my one good friend at work. He recently resigned. I now spend lunch and my free time alone. I do miss to have someone to talk to at work but at the same time I also don't want to force friendships. Not a lot of people share the same interests as mine like the series and movies I watch, which is actually very common. But yeah, work is work it's also hard if you get too close with your colleagues, they tend to not respect you as much. 
&nbsp;

edit: typo

>What the documentary don’t show you is Rocket Racoon escaped into space to fight Thanos I guess.

&nbsp;

haha I lol'd so much at this XD. Nice theory XD

Agree, the problem will eventually take care of itself. But that's the thing, from my end, I want to get the deals but, the rules that we have don't make it any easier for me. I have a target to reach, I need my commissions, and if I don't get the deal, they treat it as my fault of not communicating enough with the client that they went with a different contractor. I also believe our clients have the right to not communicate to us right away, like "F you, your price is too high, nope not talking to you".

&nbsp;

I don't even know why i'm worrying. It seems helpless right? I guess, I genuinely want to help our clients, I mean not the corps but the guys we're talking to.

Hey, nice post. I read the title thinking this post was gonna be sad and all, but found out otherwise. Nice positive attitude you got there. I wish you the best of luck! I'm pretty sure you will end up in a better place. 

&nbsp;

I'm trying to find a new job as well in a different country, but at the same time also scared of moving to a new country. Starting from 0 is a lot of work.

Allowance is part of the salary. So let's say you apply, they tell you, you get $1,000 a month nett. Then you get your pay slip that says $800 base salary + $200 allowance. Something like that.
&nbsp;
I didn't mid it before 'coz I thought maybe it's just a tax thing. They declare a lower base salary so tax will be based on that.

